Usage: gccli nutrition add --query=TEXT --meal=MEAL <date> <food-id> [flags]

Log a food of the Garmin food database in a meal. Needs Garmin Connect+.

Arguments:
  <date>       Date of the meal (YYYY-MM-DD, today, yesterday, 3d).
  <food-id>    Food ID, as nutrition search prints it.

Flags:
  -h, --help              Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json              Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain             Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header            Print the column names as the first line of --plain
                          output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"      Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING    Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"      Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                          elevations and weights in table and plain output:
                          auto (Garmin profile), metric, statute_us, statute_uk
                          ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version           Print version information.

  -q, --query=TEXT        Search text that finds the food, as you gave it to
                          nutrition search. Garmin has no read of one food by
                          ID.
  -m, --meal=MEAL         Meal: breakfast, lunch, dinner, snacks, or a custom
                          meal you enabled.
      --serving=UNIT      Serving unit, such as g or oz, or serving ID,
                          as nutrition search --json lists them under
                          nutritionContents. Defaults to the first serving of
                          the food.
      --servings=1        Number of servings.
      --time=HH:MM        Meal time (HH:MM). Defaults to the start time of the
                          meal, or to the current time for a meal without one,
                          such as snacks.

